{"id":46927049876434,"type":"album","name":"Twelve Dreams of Dr. Sardonicus","artist":"Spirit","year":1970,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710701.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-ee2973a7-14e0-48fc-8044-ffbb0a1d939e/mbid-ee2973a7-14e0-48fc-8044-ffbb0a1d939e-23117627502.png","yt":"1c0eX8Fvsmw","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/spirit/twelve-dreams-of-dr-sardonicus"},"desc":"4th LP, released in 1970 (EPIC 30267), considered as Spirit's finest work, although there was considerable friction between Randy CALIFORNIA and Jay FERGUSON at this period and it follows a more commercial rock approach. It contains a number of finely-structured rock songs like Nature's Way, Animal Zoo, Mr. Skin and Morning Will Come. There are also less structured but more ambitious numbers, such as When I Touch You and Life Has Just Begun, together with a jazzy instrumental, Space Child. The band split after the recording of this album, which was subsequently pieced together by producer David Briggs. This album ."},"artist_ref":{"id":232513413592965,"name":"The Spirit","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/d7ac95e7ce19b93dfe86e653c30cc13b/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":147423806094006,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":690,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":202159817309393,"type":"genre","name":"blues","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":444,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"}],"lists":[{"id":185548171992260,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Psychedelic Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":108,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","src":"charts","grp":"1001 Albums","list_year":null,"rank":177,"year":1970,"note":null,"total":999,"scaruffi":null},{"id":65